<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $p = \overline{p} | K$. We must show that the map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[ \phi : \calC _{\overline{p} /} \rightarrow \calC _{p/} \times _{\calD _{f \circ p/}} \calD _{f \circ \overline{p}/} \]
</div>
    <p>
       is a trivial fibration of simplicial sets. In other words, we must show that we can solve any lifting problem of the form 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { (K \star A) \coprod _{ K \star A_0} (K^{\triangleright } \star A) \ar [r] \ar @{^{(}->}[d] &amp;  \calC \ar [d]^{f} \\ K^{\triangleright } \star A \ar [r] \ar @{-->}[ur] &amp;  \calD } \]
</div>
    <p>
       Since $f$ is a left fibration, it will suffice to prove that the left vertical map is left anodyne, which follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/73DE3F" data-tag="73DE3F">4.2.3.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>